## Electromagnet sample: C-type dipole yoke (quarter model) with Kelvin spheres
## Required labels: (none)
## Optional labels: iron, air, kelvin_int, kelvin_ext
##
## Usage: Solve -> Radia-NGSolve -> Electromagnet
##
## This creates:
##   1. Iron yoke (3 volumes, quarter model, XZ symmetry)
##   2. Inner Kelvin sphere (air domain, radius 0.06 m)
##   3. Outer Kelvin sphere (copy, offset for periodic BC)

reset

# === Iron Yoke (quarter model, X=0 and Z=0 symmetry) ===

# Pole piece
brick x 0.0125 y 0.040 z 0.050
move volume 1 x 0.00625 y 0.020 z 0.025

# Yoke back
brick x 0.0125 y 0.080 z 0.025
move volume 2 x 0.00625 y 0.080 z 0.0125

# Main leg
brick x 0.0125 y 0.0625 z 0.0525
move volume 3 x 0.00625 y 0.15125 z 0.02625

imprint volume all
merge volume all

# Label iron
block 1 add volume all
block 1 name "iron"

# === Kelvin Spheres (quarter, XZ symmetry) ===
# Inner sphere: radius 0.06 m, centered at origin
# Arc from top pole (0,0,r) to equator (r,0,0), quarter-circle
create vertex 0 0 0.06
create vertex 0.06 0 0
create vertex 0 0 0
create curve arc center vertex 7 5 6
create curve vertex 5 7
create curve vertex 7 6
create surface curve 19 20 21
# Sweep 90 degrees around z-axis (quarter model)
sweep surface 19 axis 0 0 0 0 0 1 angle 90

volume 4 rename "kelvin_int"

# Outer sphere: copy + offset
volume 4 copy move x 0 y 0 z 0 nomesh
volume 5 rename "kelvin_ext"

imprint volume all
merge volume all

# === Mesh ===
volume all scheme tetmesh
volume all size 0.005
mesh volume all

# Graphics: clip plane to see interior
Graphics Clip on Plane location 0 0 0 direction 0 1 0
